# Group by Concern, Not by Type

In `setup()`, organize code by logical feature, not by reactive type. Use comments or separate composables to group related reactive state, computed, and watchers.

```javascript
setup() {
  // --- Counter feature ---
  const count = ref(0)
  const increment = () => count.value++

  // --- Search feature ---
  const search = ref('')
  const filteredItems = computed(() => items.value.filter(...))
  watch(search, () => { ... })

  return { count, increment, search, filteredItems }
}
```

Better: extract each feature into a composable.
